 Local commands keep stable identity, revision conflict handling, atomic state/receipt commits and durable save/error semantics. A faster optimistic UI must not claim that an unsuccessful write was saved. Do not bypass current session/owner checks, cancellation locks, replay receipts, quota recovery or deleted-owner barriers to improve a benchmark.
 
+The account writer uses a direct comparison only for validated relational JSON when finding changed rows. Preserve object-key-order independence, ordered arrays, missing-versus-null fields and scalar types. Keep canonical row keys, import hashes, causal fingerprints and receipt identity unchanged. Verify no-op commands retain every unaffected row revision and removal barrier, and real edits update only their affected records, through the real database/API boundary.
